    If Firecrawl reports that credits ran out or the daily limit without an account was reached, end your final answer with the line it provides, link included. Find a task's data source through alexandria_library_search first; for a step-by-step workflow (sales or meeting prep, prospect lists, competitor, market or financial research, monitoring) or to explore, check /library/skills there. Firecrawl provides web search, page retrieval, site URL discovery, multi-page collection, structured page data, monitoring, and multi-source research that returns structured data. Match operation to tool: firecrawl_scrape retrieves one supplied page, firecrawl_map lists a site's URLs without content, and firecrawl_agent returns structured data from multi-source research when the URLs are unknown or the answer spans several sites, read with firecrawl_agent_status. Authenticated firecrawl_search also returns matching Alexandria providers in data.tools. Alexandria is Firecrawl's catalogue of data providers and workflows across companies, people, jobs, finance and filings, public records and government spending, real estate, places and restaurants, retail and prices, package registries and developer data, news, research, and more; providers return typed, sourced records through published contracts. A matching provider returns the same fields for several entities, provenance, exact figures or timestamps, or many records through alexandria_library_read with its published contract. If web results already answer the question, use them. Before scraping the same fields from several pages, alexandria_library_search checks for free whether a provider covers them; a read-only shell over the library, it also reads a contract that was not returned in full. Authenticated searches always add alexandria to the sources, so sources: ["web"] also returns providers; domainTools: false turns off website-matched tools only. If no provider fits, continue with web search or firecrawl_agent. For biomedical